# state: any   (the golden cc9b4ced4a0f holds pathfind's profile; lane.accuracy804, #804, attempt 2)
# RalliSport Challenge (4D53000F): rallisport-804d.route with six screencaps during the 3-2-1
# countdown, where the owner looked for cars on the fix build and where plain1 (unfixed master)
# showed the grid cars blinking. The spare A keeps 804d's time (~+8 s after the start-race A).
# Purpose: is a rival car on screen at all, on the grid and in the pass, with the #804 fence wait
# on and off (HAKUX_OCCL_WAIT), while HAKUX_OCCL_LOG records what each visibility test returned.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
press START
wait 5
shot title
wait 3
press A
wait 6
press A
wait 6
shot mainmenu
# RIGHT exactly as pathfind sends it (pathfind.py send(): HATX max, HATX mid at once, then 0.35 s).
axis HATX max
axis HATX mid
wait 2.35
press A
wait 6
shot racetype
press A
wait 6
shot track
press A
wait 6
shot car
press A
wait 25
shot options
press A
wait 1.5
shot c1
shot c2
shot c3
shot c4
shot c5
shot c6
press A
wait 3
shot r1
shot r2
shot r3
shot r4
shot r5
shot r6
shot r7
shot r8
shot r9
shot r10
shot r11
shot r12
shot r13
shot r14
shot r15
shot r16
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    wait 20
    shot hold
}
